`consteval` makes a function an immediate function: every call must be evaluated at compile time. Which of lines A, B and C fails to compile?

```cpp
consteval int square(int x) { return x * x; }
constexpr int cube(int x)   { return x * x * x; }
int main() {
    int n = 4;
    int a = cube(n);    // A
    int b = square(3);  // B
    int c = square(n);  // C
    return a + b + c;
}
```

