On a host with 4-byte `int`, what does this print? Does `std::array` use the heap?

```cpp
#include <array>
#include <cstdio>
int main() {
    std::array<int, 4> a{1, 2, 3, 4};
    std::printf("%zu %zu\n", a.size(), sizeof(a));
    a.at(1) = 9;
    std::printf("%d %d\n", a[1], a.back());
