**Placement new** constructs an object in memory you supply, without allocating. What does this print, and what allocates the `Motor`'s memory?

```cpp
#include <cstdio>
#include <new>
struct Motor {
    int speed;
    Motor(int s) : speed(s) { std::puts("ctor"); }
    ~Motor() { std::puts("dtor"); }
};
alignas(Motor) static unsigned char slot[sizeof(Motor)];
int main() {
    Motor* m = new (slot) Motor(5);
    std::printf("%d\n", m->speed);
    m->~Motor();
}
```
